---
import GuideLayout from "../../layouts/GuideLayout.astro";
import { inr, priceOf, PACKAGES } from "../../data/pricing";
---

<GuideLayout slug="business-website-cost-india">
    <p>
        Quotes for the same business website can differ by several times, and
        the reason is rarely the design alone. Cost follows scope: how many
        pages, what features, who writes the content, and what happens after
        launch. This guide explains the pieces so you can compare quotes fairly.
        For a worked example we use our own published starting prices.
    </p>

    <h2>What drives the cost</h2>
    <ul>
        <li>
            <strong>Type of site.</strong> A simple business website with a
            few pages costs less than a product catalogue with filters and
            galleries, and far less than an online store with checkout.
        </li>
        <li>
            <strong>Number of pages and custom design.</strong> A template
            adapted to your brand is cheaper than a fully custom design.
        </li>
        <li>
            <strong>Features.</strong> Appointment booking, payment gateways,
            customer logins, multi-language support and live chat are each
            extra work.
        </li>
        <li>
            <strong>Content.</strong> Who writes the text and supplies the
            photos? Delays in content are the most common reason sites launch
            late.
        </li>
        <li>
            <strong>SEO setup.</strong> Page titles, descriptions, structured
            data, sitemap and Search Console setup are often skipped by cheap
            quotes and are hard to add later.
        </li>
        <li>
            <strong>Speed and mobile.</strong> Most visitors are on phones, so
            a site that is slow or awkward on mobile loses enquiries.
        </li>
    </ul>

    <h2>Ongoing costs people forget</h2>
    <ul>
        <li><strong>Domain name.</strong> Paid yearly, and it should be registered in your name.</li>
        <li><strong>Hosting.</strong> Included in some quotes, billed yearly in others.</li>
        <li><strong>Business email.</strong> Often separate from hosting.</li>
        <li><strong>Maintenance.</strong> Security updates, backups, fixes and content changes.</li>
        <li><strong>Marketing.</strong> A website alone does not bring visitors. Google Business Profile, SEO and ads are usually separate.</li>
    </ul>

    <h2>Example: GroverHQ starting prices</h2>
    <p>
        These are starting prices. The final quote depends on scope, and
        current prices are always on our <a href="/packages/">packages</a> and
        <a href="/services/">services</a> pages.
    </p>
    <ul>
        <li>Business website with a content management system: from {priceOf("business-website")}.</li>
        <li>Product catalogue or portfolio website: from {priceOf("catalog-website")}.</li>
        <li>Domain, email and hosting setup: from {priceOf("domain-email-hosting")}.</li>
        <li>Landing page for a campaign: from {priceOf("landing-pages")}.</li>
        <li>
            Website + Discoverability Setup, which pairs a fast SEO-ready
            website with a fully optimised Google Business Profile:
            {inr(PACKAGES.setup.price)} one-time, with the first month of
            maintenance included.
        </li>
    </ul>

    <h2>How to compare quotes</h2>
    <ol>
        <li>Ask every vendor to list pages and features so the quotes cover the same scope.</li>
        <li>Ask who owns the domain, the design files and the code.</li>
        <li>Ask what is included after launch, and what yearly fees follow.</li>
        <li>Ask how many rounds of changes are included.</li>
        <li>Ask whether SEO setup and mobile speed are part of the price.</li>
    </ol>

    <p>
        To get your business found as well as online, read our
        <a href="/guides/google-business-profile-setup-checklist/">Google Business Profile setup checklist</a>.
    </p>
</GuideLayout>
